1
00:00:00,825 --> 00:00:02,204
Last time, we asked:

2
00:00:02,224 --> 00:00:03,244
A tadpole!

3
00:00:03,544 --> 00:00:05,854
It lives in water, and it has a tail.

4
00:00:06,144 --> 00:00:07,514
What will it grow into?

5
00:00:07,566 --> 00:00:08,656
One, a fish.

6
00:00:09,906 --> 00:00:10,976
Two, a frog.

7
00:00:12,196 --> 00:00:13,526
Three, a lizard.

8
00:00:15,003 --> 00:00:16,513
Hold on to your answer!

9
00:00:18,385 --> 00:00:21,145
A little tree frog is hiding in this video.

10
00:00:21,395 --> 00:00:22,635
Can you spot it?

11
00:00:22,758 --> 00:00:25,688
Tree frogs have sticky toes, so they climb up high.

12
00:00:25,928 --> 00:00:28,108
Look on the leaves, not just in the water!

13
00:00:28,154 --> 00:00:29,614
You against the Buddies!

14
00:00:29,884 --> 00:00:31,734
Lock in first with your fingers.

15
00:00:32,004 --> 00:00:33,834
One finger for every point.

16
00:00:34,415 --> 00:00:35,565
Today you'll learn:

17
00:00:35,766 --> 00:00:37,566
The 3-stage life cycle.

18
00:00:37,771 --> 00:00:39,201
Young that look different.

19
00:00:39,406 --> 00:00:41,076
Why frog eggs have jelly.

20
00:00:41,581 --> 00:00:42,521
Are you ready?

21
00:00:42,961 --> 00:00:43,731
Three!

22
00:00:44,111 --> 00:00:44,771
Two!

23
00:00:45,141 --> 00:00:45,791
One!

24
00:00:46,211 --> 00:00:46,931
Go!

25
00:00:48,320 --> 00:00:49,210
Round one!

26
00:00:49,520 --> 00:00:51,300
What will the tadpole grow into?

27
00:00:51,590 --> 00:00:52,900
Show me your fingers!

28
00:00:56,369 --> 00:00:57,349
Locked in!

29
00:00:57,477 --> 00:01:01,177
One. It lives in water and swims with a tail, just like a

30
00:01:01,197 --> 00:01:02,037
fish.

31
00:01:02,087 --> 00:01:02,827
Three!

32
00:01:02,927 --> 00:01:05,567
It has a long tail like me, so it must grow into

33
00:01:05,587 --> 00:01:06,947
a handsome lizard!

34
00:01:06,998 --> 00:01:07,788
Two.

35
00:01:07,868 --> 00:01:10,818
Frogs sing at this pond every night, so I think it grows

36
00:01:10,838 --> 00:01:11,998
into a frog.

37
00:01:12,274 --> 00:01:14,293
But where do the tadpoles come from?

38
00:01:14,313 --> 00:01:15,153
I know!

39
00:01:15,303 --> 00:01:19,323
A mother frog has baby tadpoles, just like my mum had kittens!

40
00:01:19,977 --> 00:01:21,107
Look closer.

41
00:01:21,737 --> 00:01:25,157
Among the lily pads is a clump of clear jelly, full of

42
00:01:25,177 --> 00:01:26,652
tiny dark dots.

43
00:01:26,672 --> 00:01:28,112
Each dark dot is an egg!

44
00:01:28,302 --> 00:01:30,585
So the mother frog lays eggs, in the water.

45
00:01:30,605 --> 00:01:33,545
But why are the eggs inside all this slippery jelly?

46
00:01:33,592 --> 00:01:36,542
Frog eggs have a jelly-like covering.

47
00:01:37,112 --> 00:01:41,052
The covering protects the eggs from being eaten by other animals.

48
00:01:41,632 --> 00:01:44,132
It also keeps the eggs from drying out.

49
00:01:45,256 --> 00:01:48,276
The jelly is slippery, so a hungry fish finds it hard to

50
00:01:48,296 --> 00:01:49,226
grab an egg.

51
00:01:49,536 --> 00:01:51,826
And it holds water, so the eggs stay wet!

52
00:01:54,448 --> 00:01:55,598
Be a frog egg!

53
00:01:55,908 --> 00:01:56,898
Shrink down.

54
00:01:57,178 --> 00:01:58,108
Quietly.

55
00:02:00,395 --> 00:02:03,765
You are a tiny egg, inside the soft, clear jelly.

56
00:02:04,535 --> 00:02:06,855
A fish swims by, but you are safe.

57
00:02:07,361 --> 00:02:08,591
Days go by.

58
00:02:09,371 --> 00:02:11,051
You wriggle out of the jelly.

59
00:02:11,831 --> 00:02:15,361
You are a tadpole, with a round body and a long tail!

60
00:02:15,884 --> 00:02:17,114
Weeks go by.

61
00:02:17,884 --> 00:02:21,104
Two back legs grow out, and then two front legs.

62
00:02:21,625 --> 00:02:23,225
Your tail shrinks away.

63
00:02:24,015 --> 00:02:27,155
You climb onto a lily pad, and you breathe the air.

64
00:02:27,935 --> 00:02:29,175
You are a frog!

65
00:02:30,899 --> 00:02:32,869
The answer is two: a frog!

66
00:02:33,159 --> 00:02:34,199
Two fingers?

67
00:02:34,469 --> 00:02:35,679
One finger up!

68
00:02:35,730 --> 00:02:38,310
The young of the frog is called a tadpole.

69
00:02:39,500 --> 00:02:41,320
A tadpole is a young frog.

70
00:02:41,400 --> 00:02:44,450
It grew legs, and its tail shrank away, so now it hops

71
00:02:44,470 --> 00:02:45,610
like its parents!

72
00:02:45,662 --> 00:02:46,932
It lives in water.

73
00:02:47,242 --> 00:02:50,072
It has a tail and does not look like the adult.

74
00:02:50,803 --> 00:02:51,883
My turn!

75
00:02:52,123 --> 00:02:56,373
I drew every change: egg, tadpole, tadpole with legs, and frog.

76
00:02:56,573 --> 00:02:58,293
That is four stages!

77
00:02:58,417 --> 00:02:59,977
Something is not right.

78
00:03:00,247 --> 00:03:02,427
If you can spot it, cross your arms.

79
00:03:02,707 --> 00:03:03,667
Hold on!

80
00:03:09,080 --> 00:03:10,210
Arms crossed?

81
00:03:10,480 --> 00:03:11,690
One finger up!

82
00:03:11,742 --> 00:03:13,772
A tadpole with legs is still the young.

83
00:03:13,942 --> 00:03:16,772
It is still growing into the adult, so the frog has three

84
00:03:16,792 --> 00:03:17,812
stages!

85
00:03:20,558 --> 00:03:21,718
Say it with me!

86
00:03:22,424 --> 00:03:25,974
A life cycle with three stages includes the egg, the young and

87
00:03:25,994 --> 00:03:26,964
the adult.

88
00:03:29,587 --> 00:03:32,799
Does every young animal look so different from its parents?

89
00:03:32,819 --> 00:03:34,509
Look, a hen and her chicks!

90
00:03:34,789 --> 00:03:37,852
Some chickens walk freely near HDB blocks.

91
00:03:37,872 --> 00:03:39,792
Those chicks look nothing like the hen!

92
00:03:39,952 --> 00:03:43,302
They are small, yellow and fluffy, and she is big and brown.

93
00:03:43,957 --> 00:03:45,087
Look closer.

94
00:03:45,697 --> 00:03:47,427
Do not look only at the colour.

95
00:03:48,027 --> 00:03:49,440
Look at the body parts.

96
00:03:49,460 --> 00:03:52,250
The chick has a beak, two wings and two legs, just like

97
00:03:52,270 --> 00:03:52,960
the hen.

98
00:03:52,980 --> 00:03:55,460
And it pecks at the ground, just like its mum.

99
00:03:55,610 --> 00:03:57,725
It is a smaller, fluffier copy!

100
00:03:57,745 --> 00:04:00,555
The young of the chicken is called a chick.

101
00:04:01,945 --> 00:04:02,605
Oops!

102
00:04:02,735 --> 00:04:04,055
I only looked at the colour.

103
00:04:04,275 --> 00:04:06,815
A chick looks like the adult, the way a kitten looks like

104
00:04:06,835 --> 00:04:07,705
a cat!

105
00:04:11,402 --> 00:04:12,652
Say it with me!

106
00:04:13,362 --> 00:04:16,542
Some animals have three stages in their life cycles.

107
00:04:17,162 --> 00:04:20,252
Some of the young animals look like their parents, while some do

108
00:04:20,272 --> 00:04:20,992
not.

109
00:04:23,470 --> 00:04:24,930
Show me your score hand!

110
00:04:25,210 --> 00:04:26,600
One finger or more?

111
00:04:26,920 --> 00:04:28,280
You beat the Buddies.

112
00:04:28,550 --> 00:04:29,580
Two fingers?

113
00:04:29,860 --> 00:04:30,870
High five!

114
00:04:31,442 --> 00:04:33,132
Did you spot the tree frog?

115
00:04:33,402 --> 00:04:36,022
It was on the garden tap, beside the pond!

116
00:04:36,152 --> 00:04:37,632
Here is a fun fact!

117
00:04:37,692 --> 00:04:40,812
This tree frog lays its eggs in a ball of foam, on

118
00:04:40,832 --> 00:04:42,222
a leaf above the pond.

119
00:04:42,262 --> 00:04:45,072
When the tadpoles hatch, they drop into the water!

120
00:04:45,199 --> 00:04:46,479
Tell someone at home!

121
00:04:47,208 --> 00:04:49,408
Let's read today's key words together!

122
00:04:49,698 --> 00:04:50,458
Ready?

123
00:04:50,745 --> 00:04:52,175
Jelly-like covering.

124
00:04:53,990 --> 00:04:54,850
Tadpole.

125
00:04:56,219 --> 00:04:56,949
Chick.

126
00:04:58,215 --> 00:04:59,155
Well done!

127
00:04:59,952 --> 00:05:02,842
Look! A little grasshopper with no wings.

128
00:05:02,862 --> 00:05:05,626
And what is this empty grasshopper on the grass?

129
00:05:05,646 --> 00:05:07,236
Find out in Part Two!

130
00:05:08,396 --> 00:05:09,497
Say it with us!

131
00:05:10,297 --> 00:05:11,047
Ready?

132
00:05:11,170 --> 00:05:11,830
One!

133
00:05:12,170 --> 00:05:12,870
two!

134
00:05:13,175 --> 00:05:14,350
Now you know!
